# Students clone this on Windows, where git's default `autocrlf=true` would rewrite these
# files with CRLF line endings on checkout. bash then fails on the shebang with
# "$'\r': command not found", and GNU make appends a carriage return to every argument in
# a recipe. Both failures are baffling and neither points at line endings.
*.sh    text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.qmd   text eol=lf
*.Rmd   text eol=lf
*.ipynb text eol=lf
